WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.097
Inez scanned the pool, looking for her friend.

2
00:00:08.098 --> 00:00:11.888
"Where's Odette?" she wondered.

3
00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:15.249
Inez was with her cousin Angela.

4
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:19.981
They had come to watch Odette's swim meet.

5
00:00:19.982 --> 00:00:23.781
Right now all the swimmers were warming up.

6
00:00:23.782 --> 00:00:33.326
But Inez couldn't find Odette anywhere.

7
00:00:33.327 --> 00:00:38.286
"All the swimmers look the same," Inez complained.

8
00:00:38.287 --> 00:00:42.365
"Why do they all wear the same type of swimming gear?"

9
00:00:42.366 --> 00:00:46.895
Angela laughed. "They all want to win!

10
00:00:46.896 --> 00:00:52.819
So they wear swimsuits and caps that help them move smoothly and quickly through the water.

11
00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:59.867
Swimsuit designers even use computer programs to make the gear more efficient."

12
00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:06.782
Inez suddenly spotted her friend getting out of the pool.

13
00:01:06.783 --> 00:01:11.695
She waved. "Good luck, Odette!"

14
00:01:11.696 --> 00:01:17.508
Odette waved back before joining her Bluefish teammates.

15
00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:23.339
The youngest swimmers stood near the edge of the pool, waiting for the first event to begin.

16
00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:28.723
Inez and Angela sat down on an empty bench as the horn blew.

17
00:01:28.724 --> 00:01:33.575
"It's cool that you're on your college's swim team," Inez said.

18
00:01:33.576 --> 00:01:36.415
"I'd like to compete too."

19
00:01:36.416 --> 00:01:40.754
"Why don't you try out for the Bluefish?" Angela asked.

20
00:01:40.755 --> 00:01:48.295
Inez watched the swimmers shooting through the water.

21
00:01:48.296 --> 00:01:57.014
"Training seems hard. Besides, I love swimming, but I don't want to swim all day long!"

22
00:01:57.015 --> 00:02:01.228
"Swimmers don't just train in the water," Angela said.

23
00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:05.183
"We exercise on land too.

24
00:02:05.184 --> 00:02:09.757
I go to the gym several times a week to lift weights."

25
00:02:09.758 --> 00:02:15.623
"Oh. Do swimmers need to follow a certain diet?"

26
00:02:15.624 --> 00:02:20.733
"Nutrition is important for any athlete," Angela said.

27
00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:25.887
"Before I train or compete, I eat very carefully.

28
00:02:25.888 --> 00:02:31.888
I eat carbohydrates for energy and protein to help my muscles.

29
00:02:31.889 --> 00:02:36.040
Our trainer creates meal plans for our team.

30
00:02:36.041 --> 00:02:40.060
We get to eat a lot of pasta!"

31
00:02:40.061 --> 00:02:44.335
"I guess I could compete then," Inez said with a grin.

32
00:02:44.336 --> 00:02:51.125
"I'm very good at eating pasta! But I don't like going to bed early," she added.

33
00:02:51.126 --> 00:02:58.000
"Odette says she starts training at six in the morning."

34
00:02:58.001 --> 00:03:04.317
"Many swimmers do train first thing in the morning—that's when pools are available.

35
00:03:04.318 --> 00:03:07.921
And all athletes need a good night's sleep.

36
00:03:07.922 --> 00:03:11.559
This helps us perform our best.

37
00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:21.554
Most swimmers try to get nine or ten hours of sleep each night."

38
00:03:21.555 --> 00:03:23.836
Inez looked up.

39
00:03:23.837 --> 00:03:27.008
The next event was a relay.

40
00:03:27.009 --> 00:03:29.288
Odette stepped over to her lane.

41
00:03:29.289 --> 00:03:32.434
She was the first swimmer for the Bluefish.

42
00:03:32.435 --> 00:03:37.034
The horn blew and the swimmers dived in. Splash!

43
00:03:37.035 --> 00:03:45.826
Odette hit the water and started swimming fast, easily pulling ahead of the other racers.

44
00:03:45.827 --> 00:03:55.144
She flipped at the wall and swam back.

45
00:03:55.145 --> 00:03:59.640
The next Bluefish swimmer dived in.

46
00:03:59.641 --> 00:04:04.614
All around the pool, people clapped and cheered.

47
00:04:04.615 --> 00:04:09.657
"It does seem fun to swim on a team," Inez said.

48
00:04:09.658 --> 00:04:12.775
"It is fun," Angela said.

49
00:04:12.776 --> 00:04:15.251
Then she nudged Inez.

50
00:04:15.252 --> 00:04:19.801
"So what do you think—will you try out for the Bluefish next year?"

51
00:04:19.802 --> 00:04:24.331
"Um . . ." Inez thought for a minute and then nodded.

52
00:04:24.332 --> 00:04:32.573
"Yep, I think I'm ready to dive in!"

